Just some random thoughs of no particular value.

I've always thought that "every game is ascendable" but that "if I
really tried" I could ascend about 50% of my games.   So I decided to
"really try."

I started with Tourist and died 5 times, ascending on the 6th.

Next I tried Wizard, died *12* times, ascended on the 13th.

Next was Priest, which I very well could have ascended the first try
but died stupidly in Gehennom with a full ascention kit.  Only played
Priest once.

So I switched to the "easy" Valkerie, and died 11 times, ascended on
the 12th.  This was the most disheartening.

Looking at my logs for 2006, in 53 games I ascended 5 times, or about
10%.  So my impression of 50% is much closer to 10%, even when really
trying.

Of these deaths only three were not stupid.  One was a rolling boulder
trap on level 2. The other two were both early in the game encounters
with monsters who had picked up wands of Death and Fire and blasted me
without warning.  Maybe avoidable but at least not stupid.

I could have increased to a paltry 12% with one game where I died a few
steps from the correct altar (Pestilence got me.)

I died (on average) on level 6.6, probaby along with everybody else.
While "really trying" I average level 8.3.  I suppose I should redefine
"really try" for the tournament.

My conclusion is that by playing "perfectly" my win rate should have
been about 94%.  There is lots of room for improvement.

Greg.



